    repo: "HerJourney",
    slug: "herjourney",
    name: "HerJourney: Cycle & Health",
    tagline: "Cycle, pregnancy, menopause",
    description:
      "HerJourney is a women's health tracker that follows you through four stages of life, and keeps what you log on your own device.",
    longDescription:
      "HerJourney is a women's health tracker that follows you through four stages of life, and keeps what you log on your own device.\n\n—— Four journeys ——\n\nCYCLE\nLog periods, flow and symptoms. See where you are in your cycle — menstrual, follicular, ovulation or luteal — and what typically comes next.\n\nTRYING TO CONCEIVE\nAn ovulation calculator estimates your fertile window from your cycle length and last period.\n\nPREGNANCY\nA due-date calculator works out how far along you are and when to expect the birth, week by week.\n\nMENOPAUSE\nTrack the symptoms that matter through perimenopause and after, in the same place as everything else.\n\n—— Log what matters ——\n\n• Periods, flow and cycle length\n• Symptoms, mood and notes, day by day\n• Weight, water and the metrics you care about\n• Charts that show how things move over time\n\n—— Works with Apple Health and Health Connect ——\n\nGrant access once and HerJourney reads steps, heart rate, HRV, sleep, respiratory rate, blood oxygen, body temperature, active energy and weight, so you do not type in what your phone or watch already knows. It writes menstrual flow, water and weight back, so your other health apps stay in step. Declining leaves every other feature working.\n\n—— Your data stays with you ——\n\nEverything you log is written to a database on your device. There is no advertising SDK and no analytics SDK in the app, and nothing you log is uploaded. Signing in with Apple or Google is entirely optional and is not required to use anything.\n\n—— Not medical advice ——\n\nHerJourney is an education and self-tracking tool. It is not a medical device, it does not diagnose anything, and it is not contraception. Estimated fertile windows and due dates are calculations from the dates you enter, not clinical predictions. Talk to a clinician about any decision concerning your health.",
